title: Confront the Reaction
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: (udn_r >= 10 and coup_urgency > 1) and confronting_reaction_timer == 0 and frente_ampla_formed == 0
on-arrival: confronting_reaction_seen += 1; confronting_reaction_timer = 5; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/frente_ampla.png
tags: party_affairs; antifascism

# Confronting the Reactionary Threat

The right is on the march. The UDN and its allies in the military and the business class are openly conspiring against the constitutional order, emboldened by Washington and enraged by Goulart's reforms. Their violence in the streets grows bolder by the month.

Many in our party are demanding urgent action. The *combative* faction, centered around figures like Maurício Grabois and João Amazonas, has long argued that the Brazilian right cannot be appeased — only confronted. But voices across all tendencies are now calling for a response.

- @not_a_big_deal: The reactionaries are all bark and no bite. Let's not overreact.
- @economic_crisis
- @major_crisis: We must do something, but we are not yet ready.
- @frente_ampla

@not_a_big_deal
on-arrival: coup_urgency -= 1; left_dissent += 5; combative_dissent += 15
view-if: grabois_advisor == 0 and amazonas_advisor == 0 and giocondo_advisor == 0

The landowning class and their military friends have always rattled their sabers. Their moment will pass once the reforms begin to bite. We do not need a special strategy to confront them.

@economic_crisis
title: We must secure the Base Reforms first.
view-if: reformas_de_base == 0 and goulart_crisis_seen == 1
go-to: reformas_program

@major_crisis
view-if: coup_urgency < 5
on-arrival: coup_urgency += 1; combative_dissent -= 5; combative_strength += 5

The reactionary conspiracy is one of the gravest threats to Brazilian democracy and the popular cause. However, we are still debating our strategy and have not yet built sufficient consensus within the party or among our allies for decisive action. We must return to this.

@frente_ampla
title: Build the Broad Front!
subtitle: A united front of the PCdoB, the PTB, the CGT, the Peasant Leagues, and progressive nationalists.
view-if: coup_urgency >= 3 and frente_ampla_formed == 0
on-arrival: frente_ampla_formed = 1; radicalization += 1; coup_urgency += 1; workers_pcdo += 5*(1-dissent); peasants_pcdo += 4*(1-dissent); pro_democracy += 5*(1-dissent); left_dissent -= 8; combative_dissent -= 10; combative_strength += 5
achievement: frente_ampla_achievement

The reactionary threat can no longer be treated as a distant danger. We must build a genuine popular front — uniting the PCdoB with the labor movement, the Peasant Leagues, nationalist military officers, and all who stand to lose from a coup. The streets must become ungovernable for the right.

But around what rallying call should we organize the Front?

- @land_reform: Land reform and the Statute of the Land.
- @anti_imperialism: Nationalism and the expulsion of North American capital.
- @democracy: Defense of the constitutional order and Goulart's government.
- @armed: Arming the workers and peasants against coup plotters.
- @all_demands: All of these — an undivided program of the Brazilian people.

@land_reform
go-to: fa_end

@anti_imperialism
go-to: fa_end

@democracy
go-to: fa_end

@armed
view-if: armed_struggle_line >= 2
go-to: fa_end

@all_demands
go-to: fa_end

@fa_end

The Broad Front has breathed new life into the popular movement. For the first time in years, the left speaks with something approaching a common voice. Whether it will be enough to stop what is coming — no one can say.